version: 0.1.0

repository-code: "https://github.com/hadis-gh/chimorse"

license: GPL-3.0-or-later

keywords:
  - Python
  - computational physics
  - molecular modeling
  - chirality
  - Morse potential
  - Fourier expansion
  - anisotropic interaction potentials

abstract: >-
  ChiMorse is a Python package for constructing compact,
  symmetry-constrained Fourier–Morse representations of anisotropic pair
  interaction potentials. It provides tools for data loading, radial fitting,
  symmetry-adapted Fourier representations, optional coefficient pruning,
  model evaluation, error analysis, visualization, and model export.
